{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1","id":1005695,"title":"Examples of Time 1","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-20T07:13:45-08:00","id":1005695,"title":"Examples of Time 1","content":"So, going through the sphere descriptions for M20 and comparing it to previous editions and it got me thinking, what exactly can you accomplish with just Time 1 and no other sphere ranks?<br /> <br /> I get that you gain a really accurate clock/timer/chronometer &quot;in your head&quot; and that you can detect and analyze temporal distortions, but it seems that is really limited compared to other rank 1 spheres, so I am asking the hive mind...<br /> <br /> What else could a mage, assuming _any and/or all_ aspects/situations/circumstances were favorable, do with just Time 1 and no other spheres?<br /> <br /> Here is an example I think could work. Assuming that a mage shares their temporal sense with other (and thus both mage and target would suffer) would intentionally mucking with one's natural sense of the passage of time work? If so, this could be used from making someone late to an important meeting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12655,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","user":"tzizimine","date":". 11-20-2016, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T07:41:31-08:00","id":1005703,"title":"","content":"I had a small tirade over Time 1 on another post some time ago, so I'm just going to copy paste that here, I hope that's ok.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Time 1 is the single most underrated sphere stat in the game. Time 1 doesn't just let you know what time it is, it gives you Perfect Time Sense, you can perfectly intuit how long things take and how much time you need to do things. You know exactly when you need to get things done before the bus leaves and never miss a bus. You know exactly how much time has passed since you arrived somewhere, so no disorientation for you. You know exactly what time it is no matter where or when you are. Accidental time travel? No reading newspapers to determine the date for you, that's already covered. Captured and taken hostage for hours on end? You know exactly how long they've kept you, how long you've been travelling and how long you've been stationary, information you might need when considering an escape strategy. How about doing complicated procedures? With perfect Time Sense, you can do about 10 or so at once staggered from one another and never get a single one out of sync.<br /> <br /> With enough practice, you know exactly how long it takes to get from one place to another on various methods, and can plan your day down to the millisecond with perfect precision. No moment is wasted, and nothing is left to chance. Combined with Entropy 1, this becomes insane! You basically become Batman levels of prepared.<br /> <br /> Mixed with other spheres, you can make on going effects stop at precisely the time you intend them to, no more &quot;stop at the end of a scene, or the day&quot; now it's &quot;Stop precisely at 3pm tomorrow&quot; or &quot;Stop after exactly 15 hours&quot;. You can make Corr. gates which change location at specific times of day, Force bound temperatures that fluctuate between hot and cold depending on whether it's day or night, Spirit gates which only open for one hour at midnight. Guns that morph into gloves during the day... Any effect that you want to have multiple steps to it based on time delays needs Time 1 to pull of. Plus, with Time 1 you can sense all the temporal elements of other mage's effects. So if you come across these Time sensitive gates or items, you may not know what will happen, but you'll certainly know when it will.<br /> <br /> Also, what is the one sphere that when used, no matter how well you've planned, how much you've achieved, how many things you've accomplished, all of that can be rendered moot simply by making it all not happen? Time! What's the one point sphere that actually clues you in to when this kind of stuff is happening? Time 1! Think about it. You're in a battle and everything you throw at them, they seem to be ready for it. Any ambush, any surprise, any secret, they can react to it without a moment's hesitation. The truth is that they're using Time magic to change things to happen their way, and there is no way you could possibly know about this without Time 1. Knowing that mages are messing around with the time stream is impossible without this sphere. You don't know people are spying on you from across time, that they keep undoing your work and sabotaging your attempts before you even get a chance to pull them out of the bag. Time 1 is the only thing that might clue you in to what's going on. Without that, you're pretty much sunk. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T09:39:29-08:00","id":1005738,"title":"","content":"Thanks Saikou, and while I get the obvious benefits you pointed out, all the stuff you mentioned is either in the &quot;chronometer&quot; or &quot;detect/analyze temporal distortions&quot; (still very useful), I am wondering what else could be done with just Time 1, I.e. what other categories are there<br /> <br /> The natural time sense disruption I mentioned is kind of offensive (if very limited). Other one that came up was to tell exactly how old something is (although there is some questions on if additional rank 1 spheres are needed to get true accuracy).<br /> <br /> Another one and this goes back to share senses... Can you share your sense with an object, like you can with a person? If so, distort the quartz sensor in most digital clocks to slow/speed the vibration counter that determines how the clock knows the passage of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T09:40:18-08:00","id":1005739,"title":"","content":"While perhaps not as fervently as Saikou phrased it ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), I second the post above. Pretty much spot-on, for most cases.<br /> <br /> (EDIT:looks like we posted simultaneously... lol)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T11:18:32-08:00","id":1005769,"title":"","content":"With perfect sense of the passage of time, you become very good at music, dance, and other performances. It's like being a human metronome. Storytellers should give players difficulty reductions for such rolls when their Time 1 sense is up.<br /> <br /> Having a good grasp of time makes certain physical feats - like stunt driving or leading gunshots - similarly easier. You know that if something is moving at a constant velocity, when the exact optimal moment to act would be.<br /> <br /> Even just having Time 1 (and not using it) could aid with certain Perception rolls. In Mage: The Sorcerer's Crusade, in the Order of Reason supplement, they introduced the idea of &quot;Alertness, Awareness, or Arete?&quot;. Basically, that just having the first rank of a Sphere gives a Mage uncanny insight into subjects without rolling Arete, so long as there's a way for the character to gather said information with their mundane senses (even if that mundane sense is Awareness of supernatural presences). A person with Matter 1 or Life 1, for instance, might be much better at detecting poison in a drink than someone without them, just from rolling Perception + Alertness.<br /> <br /> Time 1 would afford the character a greater ability to determine how time has passed, relative to specific parts of the environment. It could conceivably work with Abilities other than Alertness or Awareness. With a little Medicine or Science, a Mage with Time 1 could roll them with Perception or Wits to determine how long a body has been decomposing. Science or Technology would permit them to see how long a bicycle was left outside, exposed to the elements, by the signs of visible oxidation and its mechanical features. A psychologist or therapist could use Science (Psychology) or Empathy to see how long a patient or other person has lived with certain traumas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:25:02-08:00","id":1005799,"title":"","content":"I think part of the issue with Time 1 is that while there's been plenty of awesome things posted about what it can do (though some of that can also be done with other Spheres, esp. Mind 1), is that they're largely narrative effects with little mechanical impact. At most, a lot of these things amount to a -1 to -3 difficulty break on Ability rolls that would benefit. Cool effects also don't always equate to <u>useful</u> effects in play. I think that's why most people look down on Time 1 and what it can do compared to a lot of the other Spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:52:21-08:00","id":1005819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1005799#post1005799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the issue with Time 1 is that while there's been plenty of awesome things posted about what it can do (though some of that can also be done with other Spheres, esp. Mind 1), is that they're largely narrative effects with little mechanical impact. At most, a lot of these things amount to a -1 to -3 difficulty break on Ability rolls that would benefit. Cool effects also don't always equate to <u>useful</u> effects in play. I think that's why most people look down on Time 1 and what it can do compared to a lot of the other Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Spirit 1 doesn't suffer this fate?<br /> Heck, the entire Spirit sphere relies on the whims of the ST more than any other. If you're ST doesn't know much about the other worlds or has any idea for spirits, then you're going to have a really limited scope for it all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T15:14:42-08:00","id":1005877,"title":"","content":"I don't recall arguing that Time 1 was unique in this regard. Though it suffers the worst of all of the level 1 Spheres. Entropy 1, Mind 1 (and is capable of a lot of the stuff Time 1 is), and Prime 1 are head and shoulders above the others since they have a number of specific effects that are highly practical beyond just the &quot;perception&quot; expansion thing. What has Time suffer compared to the rest of the perception focused first dots, is that its expansion of senses is mostly focused on accuracy. Correspondence lets you expand your senses around obstacles. Forces/Life/Matter all allow you to see things that would normally require bulky equipment to perceive. Spirit lets you see something mundane senses are simply incapable of seeing at all.<br /> <br /> Spirit across the board suffers more than Time (higher level of Time has a lot of concrete and useful effects) as you noted due to the much more ST dependent nature of dealing with the Umbra (though M20 made some strides to reduce this), but Time 1's esp. ST reliant. Without Time manipulations to sense, you're stuck with the &quot;perfect timing&quot; stuff, which is itself fairly ST dependent as well.<br /> <br /> To take the &quot;kidnapped&quot; scenario as an example. Time 1 lets you know exactly how long things are going on for. But you don't know what direction you're traveling in. You don't know how fast you were going. You don't know what kind of roads you were on. Trying to use time alone to aid in your rescue or escape doesn't add up to much. Correspondence 1 on the other hand would basically let you see exactly where you were the whole time and thus isn't going to require any assumptions or guesswork.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T16:02:20-08:00","id":1005892,"title":"","content":"Time 1 allows you more perception than you'd think. You can see ebbs and flows of the Timestream, this means you can see when time has been screwed around with, as well as areas where time is distorted. You'll see the trails of time travel, the residues of sped up or slowed down pockets of reality. You'll be able to see bubbles of Time affected realms within the Umbra. If Time magic has been utilised on anything at all, you'll know about it and be able to read when the trigger is meant to spring. This means being able to see things like Timed portals, Junctures, Temporary anchorheads and shallowings, as well as any kind of amulet or contingency spell, which would otherwise be invisible.<br /> <br /> You can say the same thing for every sphere.<br /> <br /> Corr 1: Without a map to explore or portals to feel out, it's basically just &quot;Where am I now?&quot;<br /> Entropy 1: Without a planned out story or fleshed out destinies, all you have is &quot;was that random?&quot; or &quot;how weak is it?&quot;<br /> Forces: 1: Without a proper understanding of physics or mystic energies, the scope of this sphere is whittled down to &quot;Do I see light? How hot is it?&quot;<br /> Life 1: Without thinking about the biology of the things the PCs may encounter, all you really have is &quot;is it alive?&quot;<br /> Matter 1: Without a comprehensive knowledge of materials, the scope is shrunk down to the level of &quot;metal, plastic, wood, or brick?&quot;<br /> Mind 1: Without an understanding of Resonance or Auras, you're pretty much limited to &quot;sense emotion&quot;.<br /> Prime 1: Without nodes and junctures, you've only really got &quot;is Magic happening?&quot;<br /> <br /> At some level, all the spheres are as effective as the ST is at providing for them.<br /> <br /> Ok, so you don't know where you are, but with Time 1 you can get a sense of your captives schedule, as well as intuit the correct rhythm to step in order to match their footsteps, walking behind them without them hearing you sneak away. What would Corr 1 give you? An incomplete map of the room. Certainly useful, but without Matter you can't look past doors without extra difficulty, without Life or Mind you can't sense the presence of guards, and without Forces you can't tell how quickly anyone is moving or whether there are any moving parts, or sounds etc. The map is good, but not great, just as good as having perfect rhythm and schedule knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T17:41:20-08:00","id":1005917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1005892#post1005892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time 1 allows you more perception than you'd think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen any case of that. You might need to recalibrate your idea of what I think.<br /> <br /> As well, a lot of your examples end up relying on other Spheres to either function at all, or would be minimally useful without them. In your latest examples, Prime 1 and Spirit 3+ would be vital to making those work. The ability to sense active Time effects on spells/other Patterns is explicitly the territory of combined effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can say the same thing for every sphere. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure which &quot;same thing&quot; we're talking about but counter examples:<br /> <br /> Correspondence 1: You can, &quot;...sense things in her immediate vicinity even if she can\u2019t perceive them with her normal senses.&quot; So if someone is hiding from you and hasn't gotten far enough away to require higher levels of Correspondence, you can find them with just this rank. You could also do things like read over someone's shoulder from across the room.<br /> <br /> Entropy 1: You can do more than &quot;was that random,&quot; and move into predicting the outcomes of random events, and you can tell if someone is lying or not (which is an extension of knowing how weak their words are, but how broadly sense weakness works without combined effects is one of the reasons its as good as it is).<br /> <br /> Forces 1: You do not need a &quot;proper understanding of physics&quot; to do more than what you propose. You can see energy that humans cannot naturally sense - such as being able to sweep a room for electronic bugs by sensing their EM signatures - and Forces 1 explicitly lets you see in the dark.<br /> <br /> Life 1: Again, you can explicitly sense more beyond &quot;is it alive,&quot; and get into specific details like age, sex, and health. As well, you can sense the presence of Life that is not normally visible to you, so you can tell if a scalpel is sterile or not by seeing if there's any Life on it.<br /> <br /> Matter 1: Explicitly grants you the knowledge about the material you say you need to make use of it... so that's not really a big deal.<br /> <br /> Mind 1: You're directly neglecting that Mind Shields, Multitasking, concealing your own aura/emotions, and temporary Mental Attribute boosting are Mind 1 effects.<br /> <br /> Prime 1: Again, you're ignoring things like Consecration and Heart's Blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At some level, all the spheres are as effective as the ST is at providing for them. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but my argument has never been some sort of silly absolutist statement that some Spheres are inherently 100% &quot;ST-proof&quot; in their utility. Since I'm not making such an argument, examples of when a given Sphere is subject to ST interpretations/whims don't really matter when I'm looking at a more holistic comparison of what they can do (and esp. do in play as opposed to in theory).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, so you don't know where you are, but with Time 1 you can get a sense of your captives schedule, as well as intuit the correct rhythm to step in order to match their footsteps, walking behind them without them hearing you sneak away. What would Corr 1 give you? An incomplete map of the room. Certainly useful, but without Matter you can't look past doors without extra difficulty, without Life or Mind you can't sense the presence of guards, and without Forces you can't tell how quickly anyone is moving or whether there are any moving parts, or sounds etc. The map is good, but not great, just as good as having perfect rhythm and schedule knowledge. </div> </div> </div>Time 1 doesn't let you sense your captives schedule. It simply gives you more information if you're trying to do ferret that out. Without an extremely good memory to track all that information, there's no guarantee you can maintain it all, while simultaneously trying to analyze it.<br /> <br /> Time 1 isn't going to turn you into a master sneak. The sound delays alone make this impossible without further stats. You'd really need Time 2 because you need to be planning your steps before the other guy has actually taken them to ensure your foot placements are timed perfectly with his to avoid being heard. And even then you're screwed the second there's a squeaky floorboard, a poorly placed mirror, or whatever to give you away.<br /> <br /> You don't need Pattern spheres to use Correspondence to see things you can't normally see... so I'm not seeing why this &quot;ineffective&quot; map stuff is coming from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T18:39:52-08:00","id":1005930,"title":"","content":"I typically just give my players a pychometry like effect to compensate(player can see events in the past of a object/person that have a strong metaphysical significance), and leave future sight to sphere two. It's just a little progressive ability like how correspondence gives you 360 degree night vision that can be around or through objects at dot 1, and the clairvoyant ability to see anywhere at sphere 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 11-20-2016, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T18:58:09-08:00","id":1005936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1005917#post1005917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't seen any case of that. You might need to recalibrate your idea of what I think.<br /> <br /> As well, a lot of your examples end up relying on other Spheres to either function at all, or would be minimally useful without them. In your latest examples, Prime 1 and Spirit 3+ would be vital to making those work. The ability to sense active Time effects on spells/other Patterns is explicitly the territory of combined effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sure which &quot;same thing&quot; we're talking about but counter examples:<br /> <br /> Correspondence 1: You can, &quot;...sense things in her immediate vicinity even if she can\u2019t perceive them with her normal senses.&quot; So if someone is hiding from you and hasn't gotten far enough away to require higher levels of Correspondence, you can find them with just this rank. You could also do things like read over someone's shoulder from across the room.<br /> <br /> Entropy 1: You can do more than &quot;was that random,&quot; and move into predicting the outcomes of random events, and you can tell if someone is lying or not (which is an extension of knowing how weak their words are, but how broadly sense weakness works without combined effects is one of the reasons its as good as it is).<br /> <br /> Forces 1: You do not need a &quot;proper understanding of physics&quot; to do more than what you propose. You can see energy that humans cannot naturally sense - such as being able to sweep a room for electronic bugs by sensing their EM signatures - and Forces 1 explicitly lets you see in the dark.<br /> <br /> Life 1: Again, you can explicitly sense more beyond &quot;is it alive,&quot; and get into specific details like age, sex, and health. As well, you can sense the presence of Life that is not normally visible to you, so you can tell if a scalpel is sterile or not by seeing if there's any Life on it.<br /> <br /> Matter 1: Explicitly grants you the knowledge about the material you say you need to make use of it... so that's not really a big deal.<br /> <br /> Mind 1: You're directly neglecting that Mind Shields, Multitasking, concealing your own aura/emotions, and temporary Mental Attribute boosting are Mind 1 effects.<br /> <br /> Prime 1: Again, you're ignoring things like Consecration and Heart's Blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, but my argument has never been some sort of silly absolutist statement that some Spheres are inherently 100% &quot;ST-proof&quot; in their utility. Since I'm not making such an argument, examples of when a given Sphere is subject to ST interpretations/whims don't really matter when I'm looking at a more holistic comparison of what they can do (and esp. do in play as opposed to in theory).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Time 1 doesn't let you sense your captives schedule. It simply gives you more information if you're trying to do ferret that out. Without an extremely good memory to track all that information, there's no guarantee you can maintain it all, while simultaneously trying to analyze it.<br /> <br /> Time 1 isn't going to turn you into a master sneak. The sound delays alone make this impossible without further stats. You'd really need Time 2 because you need to be planning your steps before the other guy has actually taken them to ensure your foot placements are timed perfectly with his to avoid being heard. And even then you're screwed the second there's a squeaky floorboard, a poorly placed mirror, or whatever to give you away.<br /> <br /> You don't need Pattern spheres to use Correspondence to see things you can't normally see... so I'm not seeing why this &quot;ineffective&quot; map stuff is coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Couple of points<br /> <br /> 1. well, if you're going to decide that certain effects with Time 1 are impossible without other spheres, then yes, you're going to have Time 1 be unusable on its own. Specifically regarding the Time 4 style effects or amulets, you shouldn't need any other sphere to know there's a time effect going and when it will go off. Similarly, you can be able to feel the distortion in temporal space that such time related things as shallowings, junctures, and the rest of it. You might not be able to identify what this disturbance is without the other spheres, but you'll be able to detect the disturbance.<br /> <br /> 2. the &quot;same thing&quot; is in reference to the point that every sphere requires a level of ST understanding or things in order for the sphere to be properly utilised. If your ST doesn't understand concepts like &quot;pressure&quot; or &quot;radiation&quot; then certain Forces effects are not going to be possible to do. So if your ST doesn't know about EM signatures, it's going to be harder to use Forces to search for them than if you had a ST who did. That's all. It's not a phenomenon unique to Time or Spirit. If you're ST isn't clued up, then you're going to have a hard time working them into the story without a lot of negotiation.<br /> <br /> 3. Didn't ignore, just either forgot or paraphrased for the sake of making the initial point. It's not about what the spheres are capable of, it's that the ST's understanding of the things the spheres control will be the upper limit on what the spheres can do.<br /> <br /> 4. You don't need all that good a memory when you can feel it out, that's the whole benefit of perfect time sense, sensing tracks of time becomes like seeing colour to you. You just know how much time has passed and the intervals between things and how often they occur from what you have witnessed. To say you can keep track of this and analyse is not unlike saying you can't remember what colours you're holding while colouring between the lines.<br /> <br /> 5. Sound delays can be accounted for with time 1, delays of any kind can be sensed and adjusted for with Time 1 actually, that's kind of thing fits into Perfect Time Sense quite nicely, all you need do is observe them for a while, pick up their rhythm, and match it down to the millisecond. Ok, you've mentioned the limitations of this technique, not sure how that invalidates it though...<br /> <br /> 6. Yes you do, this isn't Corr 2 where you're pushing out your senses, this is Corr 1 where it's nothing but feeling out a room sonar style. All you get is the spatial layout of the area. You are unable to distinguish between matter and life, and you certainly can't see through matter or life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T22:02:00-08:00","id":1005983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1005936#post1005936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, if you're going to decide that certain effects with Time 1 are impossible without other spheres, then yes, you're going to have Time 1 be unusable on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you might want to reread the text? Because regardless of why you're saying these things, they're wrong. I'm not deciding this, the text says:<br /> <br /> &quot;Combined with additional Spheres, this Rank allows the mage to detect the influence of the Time Sphere on other spells or Patterns too.&quot; M20, page. 522.<br /> <br /> If you want to house rule it, I'm all for it, because I find Time 1 RAW a bit silly (as I thought was clearly) in how limited it is. But don't tell me I'm making up restrictions to make it worse than it is, when the restrictions I'm referencing are straight out of the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the &quot;same thing&quot; is in reference to the point that every sphere requires a level of ST understanding or things in order for the sphere to be properly utilised. </div> </div> </div>I never said &quot;understanding.&quot; STs can defer to players on topics of out-of-character knowledge. I said dependent because the ST is the ultimate arbiter of rules calls regardless of how they reach their decision. Maybe a matter of different experiences, but since creative magic in Mage usually means some degree of negotiation, Mage STs generally don't pull things like, &quot;well, I have no idea about how EM emissions by electronics work, so you can't use Forces 1 to scan the room for them.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not about what the spheres are capable of, it's that the ST's understanding of the things the spheres control will be the upper limit on what the spheres can do. </div> </div> </div>The text has plenty to say on what each ranking in a Sphere should allow.<br /> <br /> As well, I've already been fairly direct that this attempt to force a false dichotomy on this point of contention is misplaced. You using arguments that only work if you insist that there is no scaling in how much ST dependent rulings impact each Sphere/Sphere rank; that since all of them have some, that value is inherently equal. This clearly is not backed up by the text, and doesn't even follow some of your own statements from up thread.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, all this sort of thing really comes down to is that Time 1 is either useful because you're house ruling it to be better, or equal to the others in utility because you're house ruling them to be worse. You're not demonstrating that Time 1 is actually better than it looks RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't need all that good a memory when you can feel it out, that's the whole benefit of perfect time sense, sensing tracks of time becomes like seeing colour to you. </div> </div> </div>Please cite the text that supports this. Time 1 gives you a perfect internal clock, and lets you detect distortions to the time stream around you. Nothing in the text says you can &quot;see&quot; people's schedules with Time 1 alone; those aren't distortions to the time-stream. It's also called &quot;Time Sense,&quot; not, &quot;Perfect Time Sense.&quot; Perfect only applies to your internal clock effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You just know how much time has passed and the intervals between things and how often they occur from what you have witnessed. </div> </div> </div>How exactly do you witness any of this? You only know what you can see. You can't track different people with Time 1 to know if one person always goes out for a drive every morning ~9 AM and returns in ~1 hour, or if they rotate. You can't say what that person is doing while they're gone for an hour; if it's the same thing or different things. Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To say you can keep track of this and analyse is not unlike saying you can't remember what colours you're holding while colouring between the lines. </div> </div> </div>It's extremely unlike that. It's more like trying to remember your meals every day and try to calculate your nutritional input, from memory alone. Unlike the coloring between the lines situation, you don't have a visual aid to remind you of your past work, a set of crayons/markets/pens/etc. to reference, and you're doing it over a prolonged period of time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sound delays can be accounted for with time 1, delays of any kind can be sensed and adjusted for with Time 1 actually, that's kind of thing fits into Perfect Time Sense quite nicely, all you need do is observe them for a while, pick up their rhythm, and match it down to the millisecond. Ok, you've mentioned the limitations of this technique, not sure how that invalidates it though... </div> </div> </div>Nothing in Time 1 actually says you can perceive natural delays. If you were following a robot with a steady consistent gait, matching it's rhythm with an offset for the delay in sound waves getting to the robot's aural sensors, that might be feasible. With a living person they aren't going to walk with a perfect gait, and without the ability to predict irregularities before they happen, you'll be unable to adjust fast enough physically (even if you could know you have to mentally + Time 1) to avoid falling out of step.<br /> <br /> What you seem to be forgetting is that for this to work, your feet need to hit the ground <b>before</b> their feet do, so that the sound of your foot step hits their ears at the same time as theirs. If you step at the same time as them exactly, you'll create an audible irregularity (probably heard as an echo which could be very jarring unless the space is already prone to echoes).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. Yes you do, this isn't Corr 2 where you're pushing out your senses, this is Corr 1 where it's nothing but feeling out a room sonar style. All you get is the spatial layout of the area. You are unable to distinguish between matter and life, and you certainly can't see through matter or life. </div> </div> </div>I've quote the book already. You're wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T01:54:13-08:00","id":1006066,"title":"","content":"I'm on the fence myself, regarding just how extensive the sensory impressions of Correspondence 1 are.<br /> <br /> I've always read it RAW as sensing literal space around you - enough to detect the exact shapes of everything around, which is usually enough to notice attackers, objects, notice sudden motion and what have you, but not enough to discern something like actual text on a digital screen, or listening in on somebody's talk.<br /> <br /> Because if you say that, yes, Correspondence 1 extends all normal senses around you, you not only get sight, but also sound, feeling, tasting etc., which makes Correspondence 1...seriously powerful without the use of any other spheres.<br /> <br /> I see it more as the mother of all super-resolution echolocations.<br /> The RAW supports this idea, as the examples of things you can notice with the first level of Correspondence are all the kind of things you would notice by having an intricate knowledge of space and/or lack of space around you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-21-2016, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T05:49:26-08:00","id":1006150,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> The problem i have with your interpretation of Corr vs your interpretation of Time is that you claim Time 1 requires other spheres to do anything outside of its two given rotes, while Corr 1 can do anything without need of help. There's a contradiction in place, because if you state that Corr is able to sense all other patterns without needing their sphere, but Time isn't capable of sensing time based magics like timed portals, Amulets, or similarly programmed events without other spheres, then you are giving Corr an inherent bias.<br /> If you want to rely on &quot;that's what the book says, therefor it right&quot; then you do the whole sphere system a disservice.<br /> <br /> At its core, the sphere system is meant to be a level of guidelines to give you a rough idea on how to approach their use in magic. It is the limits of our ingenuity as well as our ability to see the patterns presented by both our mages paradigm and the spheres convention that should dictate what is and isn't possible, not just &quot;well if you look at page 39, it clearly says it's only thing&quot;.<br /> <br /> I had a game where an ST allowed Time 4/Entropy 1 to be used to &quot;save your game&quot;, basically making a reference point in time which you'd jump back to in the event of the players death. The idea was that they imagined time as a stream, and Time 4 allowed you to bend that stream around things or places, so the logical conclusion is that you could bend it so far that it actually meets itself, like a piece of string making a knot.<br /> <br /> No where is that in the book, not even under Time 5. Instead Time 5 would cut through that process of having to prepare a &quot;checkpoint&quot; before hand, and just allow you to jump without need of worry.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I've had a game where someone was able to change their hair colour with Life 2. If you go RAW then only Life 3 should allow &quot;alter self&quot; type effects, but if we're going to lump &quot;giving myself claws&quot; with &quot;changing my hair from red to blond&quot; and say &quot;sorry, you may be able to manipulate plants, but your hair colour is just too advanced for you&quot; doesn't that get a little silly?<br /> <br /> If your main argument against doing new and interesting thing with the spheres is &quot;the book doesn't say anything about that&quot; then you're basically treating the game like so many over List based magic systems in which you need a defined rote before an effect can take place.<br /> <br /> We could, for example, say a good Time 1 effect should give you an extra success or a reduced difficulty on Dexterity based things, such as dodging or fighting because you can feel the perfect time to move and can sense the pattern in your enemy's fire, but if you say &quot;book doesn't talk about that, so no&quot; then of course it's not going to fly.<br /> <br /> The rotes are meant to be examples and ideas from which to build from, not hammered down &quot;this is how one does magic&quot;. The descriptions of the spheres gives you an idea, a feel for how the relative powers of the spheres would work. Yes there are many different ways to approach a given solution, but that does not mean other methods are suddenly invalid. To say &quot;you can use mind to do all the Time 1 stuff&quot; doesn't suddenly mean that Time 1 can't do this stuff or that Mind 1 is better at doing this stuff than Time 1. Such exclusive thinking can only harm ones creativity as it denies the possibility of the unexpected.<br /> <br /> If you're playing a game in which every spell needs to be taken from a source or double checked with HDYDT, then I'd say you're being far too rigid in your approach to this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T06:55:10-08:00","id":1006171,"title":"","content":"So to summarize what has mentioned so far, I see four distinct categories for Time 1 (and again only Time 1)<br /> <br /> 1. Detect / Analyze Temporal Distortion (covering time travel, time scrying, time loops, etc)<br /> 2. Perfect Chronometer (covering accurate passage and measurement of time, which, personally, I can see helping with Ability checks when coordination or timing with something already perceived is important, but not with unknown schedules, plans, intentions or other occurrences not yet observed... That's where Time 2, Entropy or Mind start get involved)<br /> 3. Detect / Analyze Age (knowing exactly how old something is by seeing how much of the time stream that pattern has been exposed to)<br /> 4. Adjust Natural Time Sense (mess with another's ability to gauge time. Very limited as it would have to be willing and via touch, but if we can get an answer about if sharing senses with objects, it could still be useful to mess with clocks)<br /> <br /> So, are there any other _categories_, not specific examples that anyone else can think of.<br /> <br /> (I.e. I am not wanting an exchanges on if specific effect X could/couldn't work with just Time 1. That will always be up for ST approval and house rules. I am looking for whole new categories)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T07:05:02-08:00","id":1006175,"title":"","content":"Sphere level interpretation always varies by ST. And I agree that Time 1 gets seriously shafted in relation to other level 1s. Most my players dont even bother as long as 1 gets Time to level 2 for a bit of postcognition. <br /> <br /> 1 thing I tend to do with all levels is to look at the weakest effect the next level of a sphere is required for, then everything weaker than that falls in the previous sphere influence. Under this idea most of what is being suggested by Saikou would be relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T13:03:51-08:00","id":1006352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006150#post1006150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> The problem i have with your interpretation of Corr vs your interpretation of Time is that you claim Time 1 requires other spheres to do anything outside of its two given rotes, while Corr 1 can do anything without need of help.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book says. The book makes the applications of the Spheres uneven. If you have a problem with it, house rule it. I'm all for that. But don't say I'm doing something wrong, or causing issues, when the text is clear on these things.<br /> <br /> Also Corr 1 can't do &quot;anything&quot; without the need of help. You can't perceive anything your normal senses couldn't perceive naturally if that subject was right in front of them. It simply allows you to perceive around yourself despite spatial obstructions. You don't need to combine Corr 1 with Matter to see &quot;through&quot; a wall because you're not actually seeing &quot;through&quot; the wall, you're seeing &quot;around&quot; the wall. Just like with Corr 2 you don't need to combine Spheres to scry a far away location. You can look around another place all you want with just Corr 2.<br /> <br /> You combine with Corr when you want to see things beyond your normal senses (like Prime 1 to see auras) or start affecting things you see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to rely on &quot;that's what the book says, therefor it right&quot; then you do the whole sphere system a disservice. </div> </div> </div>Not really. If there's a disservice being done, it's by the book, not by me.<br /> <br /> And if we get to ignore the book, then there's no point in any of this as a conversation. If we're ignoring the book I can just say that Time 1 sucks because if you don't spend 1 XP per success Time 1 stops working automatically. It doesn't matter that the book doesn't say how things work, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At its core, the sphere system is meant to be a level of guidelines to give you a rough idea on how to approach their use in magic. It is the limits of our ingenuity as well as our ability to see the patterns presented by both our mages paradigm and the spheres convention that should dictate what is and isn't possible, not just &quot;well if you look at page 39, it clearly says it's only thing&quot;. </div> </div> </div>This is a false dichotomy. The game is a combination of creativity and rules. Creativity is fine, but if the book says, &quot;you need to combine Spheres with Time 1 to do X,&quot; you don't get to just ignore that. It doesn't mean Time 1 can't do anything without combining Spheres, but that specific thing is not a &quot;Time 1 only&quot; thing. You're trying to make this too much of either, &quot;you have to be super flexible!&quot; or, &quot;you're too literal!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, I've had a game where someone was able to change their hair colour with Life 2. If you go RAW then only Life 3 should allow &quot;alter self&quot; type effects, but if we're going to lump &quot;giving myself claws&quot; with &quot;changing my hair from red to blond&quot; and say &quot;sorry, you may be able to manipulate plants, but your hair colour is just too advanced for you&quot; doesn't that get a little silly? </div> </div> </div>Not to me. But I'm a biologist and claws are actually easier than changing hair color in terms of how much you're actually changing. Of course, I'd allow other options (like a Matter/Life combo) to do something like a perfect instant dye-job.<br /> <br /> Getting into the &quot;well this is mechanically weaker application of a Sphere X effect, so knock down the requirement,&quot; mentality gets messy fast with players that know what they're doing. It can very quickly turn into getting higher level effects with multiple small applications of &quot;reduced requirement&quot; effects (which also means they're lower base difficulty). There are always &quot;vanity&quot; applications of higher effects, throwing away the requirements because of them just makes things messy and harder to adjudicate. There are other things in the game for this (like the required base successes for changing your hair being lower than growing claws even if both take Life 3).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your main argument against doing new and interesting thing.... </div> </div> </div>I have made no such argument.<br /> <br /> I've argued solely against the specific Sphere requirements you've posited for specific effects (some of which are directly from the book, and some aren't). The books don't say anything about using Time to try to match someone's footsteps to avoid making sound they can hear. I think it's a neat idea. I just don't think it's a Time 1 effect based on what you need to make it work. The descriptions of Time 1, and Time 2, and the effect attempting to achieve, make it very clearly fall into Time 2 or combination effects. Same with the &quot;combat timing&quot; stuff. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're playing a game in which every spell needs to be taken from a source or double checked with HDYDT, then I'd say you're being far too rigid in your approach to this game. </div> </div> </div>If you're trying to have a civil conversation, how about not trying to hide childish barbs behind &quot;if&quot; statements?<br /> <br /> Or if you're simply going to resort to insults when your ideas are challenged, tell me that so I don't waste my time responding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tzizimine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006171#post1006171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Detect / Analyze Age (knowing exactly how old something is by seeing how much of the time stream that pattern has been exposed to)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure this category works with just Time 1. The metaphysics of the game aren't posited such that chronological age is a result of &quot;time stream exposure.&quot; Noticing that something is out-of-sync with the time-stream and isn't the age it appears would (but that's just category #1 rephrased). It also presumes that time is a constant so a 5 year old, a 10 year old, and a 20 year old are exposed to a reliably quantifiable amount of &quot;time stream.&quot;<br /> <br /> For an example, you can't use Matter to see how old a living tree is by sensing the grow ring patterns. You need Life to do that. Though those reverse with a dead tree. It doesn't matter that the ring patterns are a purely physical arrangement of matter, because they're bound up in a living pattern <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, are there any other _categories_, not specific examples that anyone else can think of. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it would count as a separate category from #1, but sensing natural time dilation via relativity should fall in here somewhere. Time 1 should allow you to combine your perfect internal chronometer with the ability to sense distortions to leave you able to recognize the difference it &quot;actual time&quot; based on that chronometer vs. the small natural changes that result from normally imperceptible dilation effects that happen all around us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T14:18:14-08:00","id":1006390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006352#post1006352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book says. The book makes the applications of the Spheres uneven. If you have a problem with it, house rule it. I'm all for that. But don't say I'm doing something wrong, or causing issues, when the text is clear on these things.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Ok, nevermind then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006352#post1006352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Corr 1 can't do &quot;anything&quot; without the need of help. You can't perceive anything your normal senses couldn't perceive naturally if that subject was right in front of them. It simply allows you to perceive around yourself despite spatial obstructions. You don't need to combine Corr 1 with Matter to see &quot;through&quot; a wall because you're not actually seeing &quot;through&quot; the wall, you're seeing &quot;around&quot; the wall. Just like with Corr 2 you don't need to combine Spheres to scry a far away location. You can look around another place all you want with just Corr 2.<br /> <br /> You combine with Corr when you want to see things beyond your normal senses (like Prime 1 to see auras) or start affecting things you see.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I think we've been talking cross purposes on this matter. I've been imagining the Corr 1 effect of &quot;Landscape of the Mind&quot; in which you can feel out the space around you, HUD style. It's not so much a question of getting around a wall, but rather of being able to see inside, say closed drawers. You know, how detailed this mental blueprint becomes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006352#post1006352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. If there's a disservice being done, it's by the book, not by me.<br /> <br /> And if we get to ignore the book, then there's no point in any of this as a conversation. If we're ignoring the book I can just say that Time 1 sucks because if you don't spend 1 XP per success Time 1 stops working automatically. It doesn't matter that the book doesn't say how things work, right?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> That's a rather all or nothing approach, wouldn't you say? I do not wish to say the book should be ignored, but rather that what isn't in the book shouldn't be dismissed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006352#post1006352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a false dichotomy. The game is a combination of creativity and rules. Creativity is fine, but if the book says, &quot;you need to combine Spheres with Time 1 to do X,&quot; you don't get to just ignore that. It doesn't mean Time 1 can't do anything without combining Spheres, but that specific thing is not a &quot;Time 1 only&quot; thing. You're trying to make this too much of either, &quot;you have to be super flexible!&quot; or, &quot;you're too literal!&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why you think Time 1 would not be enough to sense when a Time 4 spell has been cast, or when something that makes a disruption in the time stream, like a Juncture, or a shallowing. Sure you'll need other spheres to feel out what the Time 4 spell is holding, and what this disruption in the time stream actually is (prime for junctures, spirit for shallowings), but you should still be able to sense the preverbial &quot;something&quot; in the area, and perhaps be able to determine at least in part the timing of it all.<br /> What's wrong with that as an interpretation of Time Sense?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006352#post1006352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to me. But I'm a biologist and claws are actually easier than changing hair color in terms of how much you're actually changing. Of course, I'd allow other options (like a Matter/Life combo) to do something like a perfect instant dye-job.<br /> <br /> Getting into the &quot;well this is mechanically weaker application of a Sphere X effect, so knock down the requirement,&quot; mentality gets messy fast with players that know what they're doing. It can very quickly turn into getting higher level effects with multiple small applications of &quot;reduced requirement&quot; effects (which also means they're lower base difficulty). There are always &quot;vanity&quot; applications of higher effects, throwing away the requirements because of them just makes things messy and harder to adjudicate. There are other things in the game for this (like the required base successes for changing your hair being lower than growing claws even if both take Life 3).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> So it would be harder to change hair colour, and may require matter magic, for those with a paradigm befitting a biologist, or at least someone who knew the science behind hair. For more primordial paradigms, say like a Verbena, I don't think such a restriction would apply. For them the hair that grows on their head would be as simple to manipulate as the grass that grows at their feet. For them, life is life afterall, and they'd probably say it's Technocracy that tries to reduce and categorise everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006352#post1006352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have made no such argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh good.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006352#post1006352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've argued solely against the specific Sphere requirements you've posited for specific effects (some of which are directly from the book, and some aren't). The books don't say anything about using Time to try to match someone's footsteps to avoid making sound they can hear. I think it's a neat idea. I just don't think it's a Time 1 effect based on what you need to make it work. The descriptions of Time 1, and Time 2, and the effect attempting to achieve, make it very clearly fall into Time 2 or combination effects. Same with the &quot;combat timing&quot; stuff.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> The way I imagine a lot of Perfect Time style effects working is by making you not unlike Temple Fugate from that Bataman Animated Series, where he can dodge every punch thrown at him because he can feel exactly when he has to move in order to doge it. I'd translate that into this game as a Dex boost, or at the very least a dodge boost. Saying &quot;nah, you need Time 2 for that&quot; seems a bit stingy to me.<br /> <br /> I mean, what would you use Time 1 Perfect Time for if you had to &quot;know the future&quot; for any of this stuff to work?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006352#post1006352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're trying to have a civil conversation, how about not trying to hide childish barbs behind &quot;if&quot; statements?<br /> <br /> Or if you're simply going to resort to insults when your ideas are challenged, tell me that so I don't waste my time responding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm... Didn't intend for that last sentence to come across as an insult, sorry about that.<br /> I'm just trying make the point that if the sphere magic must be &quot;back'ed up&quot; by the books before it can be deemed allowable, then what good does that do the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 11-21-2016, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T15:57:02-08:00","id":1006443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006390#post1006390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI think we've been talking cross purposes on this matter. I've been imagining the Corr 1 effect of &quot;Landscape of the Mind&quot; in which you can feel out the space around you, HUD style.</div> </div> </div> </div>You.. .realize you're basically saying that your counter-argument is based on exactly what you've accused me of doing? I've been looking at the general descriptions of what the different levels of Correspondence can do, and extrapolating from there, while you're countering with a single Rote as to why I'm overstating what Corr 1 can do.<br /> <br /> When I'm looking at Time, I'm doing the same thing. I'm looking at what the books say Time 1 and Time 2 do, and then seeing where something that's not already a rote would fall within what those write-ups say.<br /> \u200b<br /> I'm not &quot;dismissing&quot; something that's not in the book. I'm arguing that it has to be weighed against what is in the book. If the books says you need Time 1 + another Sphere for something, something not in the book doesn't get to go around that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure why you think Time 1 would not be enough to sense when a Time 4 spell has been cast, or when something that makes a disruption in the time stream, like a Juncture, or a shallowing. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say anything contrary to this. Though shallowings aren't inherently time disrupting so would be out because of that, and Junctures could be sensed with Spirit as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So it would be harder to change hair colour, and may require matter magic, for those with a paradigm befitting a biologist, or at least someone who knew the science behind hair. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say I'd require Matter. I said I'd allow a Matter/Life option instead of Life 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For more primordial paradigms, say like a Verbena, I don't think such a restriction would apply. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Verbena would just follow that it's Life 3 and probably wouldn't do the &quot;Matter dye-job,&quot; thing if they're more old school about these things (though there are plenty of examples in the books of Verbena that are also scientists and most Verbena would understand that how complicated life can be is not always readily apparent).<br /> <br /> Paradigms don't let you reduce the Sphere requirements for an effect, even if they might open up alternate paths to get the same results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way I imagine a lot of Perfect Time style effects working is by making you not unlike Temple Fugate from that Bataman Animated Series, where he can dodge every punch thrown at him because he can feel exactly when he has to move in order to doge it. </div> </div> </div>Baring the original Clock King, all of the versions of this character which follow the same style (Clock King II in the comics and the Flash TV show version) explicitly call this out as a form of precognition, and in the DCAU he eventually powers up significantly with a time dilating gadget... so maybe not the best example?<br /> <br /> There's a lot of tricks he pulls (like knowing the train schedules so well that he can time jumping onto one before it's come into view) could be done with a mixture of Time 1 + high stats + some luck that today isn't the day the train is late.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, what would you use Time 1 Perfect Time for if you had to &quot;know the future&quot; for any of this stuff to work? </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that's why a lot of people find Time 1 to be so disappointing RAW. If the books supported some sort of &quot;spidey-sense&quot; level stuff (like the CofD did with Time 1), it would be a lot cooler and a lot more applicable. But as written any level of pre-cog starts at Time 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm just trying make the point that if the sphere magic must be &quot;back'ed up&quot; by the books before it can be deemed allowable, then what good does that do the game? </div> </div> </div>The books are the common ground we all operate on. As noted earlier, it's still got to follow the Sphere write-ups if there isn't an official rote for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T17:40:25-08:00","id":1006480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006443#post1006443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You.. .realize you're basically saying that your counter-argument is based on exactly what you've accused me of doing? I've been looking at the general descriptions of what the different levels of Correspondence can do, and extrapolating from there, while you're countering with a single Rote as to why I'm overstating what Corr 1 can do.<br /> <br /> When I'm looking at Time, I'm doing the same thing. I'm looking at what the books say Time 1 and Time 2 do, and then seeing where something that's not already a rote would fall within what those write-ups say.<br /> \u200b<br /> I'm not &quot;dismissing&quot; something that's not in the book. I'm arguing that it has to be weighed against what is in the book. If the books says you need Time 1 + another Sphere for something, something not in the book doesn't get to go around that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for misunderstanding your statements. Now if I do the same for Time 1 I see this:<br /> &quot;Natural phenomena sometimes cause odd Time distortions, too, and these are apparent to a trained mage.&quot; Right, so what could these natural phenomena be? One thing could be naturally occuring Junctures, another could be time related shallowings, i.e. shallowings that only come into being at midnight, or on thursdays (for whatever reason).<br /> Another thing this hints at is naturally occurring time portals or time eddies. Perhaps that moment of De Ja Vu had more going on than you'd first assume.<br /> <br /> Looking at what's said in the Perfect Time rote:<br /> &quot;Only Time magic can sense and correct for distortions in subjective time.&quot; That sounds to me like being able to use this trick to get around the delays caused by perception.<br /> &quot;The mage can keep absolute track of her own Effects and timing, easily judging subjective time as necessary to put a precise duration or spin on any action.&quot;<br /> I take this to mean if you need to stop on a dime, then you can, so if you're following someone and they stop moving, you can stop along with them. If you're trying to shoot someone just as they move their arm to shoot you, you get them just that moment before they have a chance to reach their gun.<br /> The distortion in subjective time caused by perception and reaction are no longer a problem depending on the intensity of this effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006443#post1006443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Verbena would just follow that it's Life 3 and probably wouldn't do the &quot;Matter dye-job,&quot; thing if they're more old school about these things (though there are plenty of examples in the books of Verbena that are also scientists and most Verbena would understand that how complicated life can be is not always readily apparent).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure there are many example of such Verbena, but for the purposes of the example I was trying to demonstrate, I wasn't focusing on them at this time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006443#post1006443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradigms don't let you reduce the Sphere requirements for an effect, even if they might open up alternate paths to get the same results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, see I would disagree with this point quite a bit. Paradigm defines what it is you consider each kind of pattern to be, and so which spheres you require to manipulate them will be very much based on this.<br /> <br /> For example. You need Force 2 to amplify forces, and Forces 3 to change them.<br /> Let's look at a Hermetic, he believes that Light and Dark are separate opposing energies. in order to change Dark into Light he'd need Forces 3, but with Forces 2, he would be able to move the Darkness around, and maybe even drape the Dark around them, wearing it like a cloak.<br /> Now let's look at an Etherite, she believes that light is basically Photons, and dark is just the absence of Photons. To her, changing Dark into Light would be Forces 2 since all she's doing is moving photons around, however she wouldn't be able to do that were &quot;wear the darkness&quot; thing that the Hermetic was doing since Darkness isn't actually a thing.<br /> <br /> Take another example, Entropy 1 to see sense Entropy, Entropy 2 to affect pure Entropy.<br /> The scenario is being trying to escape a building with Entropy.<br /> We have a Verbena who believes in fate. She thinks she is destined to escape, so all she needs to do is Entropy 1 to read her path and intuit how to leave.<br /> We have a Hollow One who considers all forms of order to be little more than a lie, the universe is chaos and fate doesn't exist. If they're getting out, it's by controlling this chaos and forcing a route, they do Entropy 2 to force circumstance to give them a route. Can't use Entropy 1 for this, since there's nothing to read. If they wanted to use Entropy 1 it would be for reading the chaos in places. Entropy 2 for our Verbena would be magic which is able to alter one's fate in slight ways. There is no chance to her, only the realisation of what the universe has in store for you.<br /> We have a Virtual Adept who doesn't believe in fate or subscribe to a worldview of chaos, but instead considers all things as a product of simple statistics. Entropy 1 is then crunching the numbers in order to figure out the most efficient route, while Entropy 2 would be a method by which you can calculate how you may lower or raise the probability escaping without getting caught, for instance. The way the VA views the results would be different too. The Verbena would walk down their path and feel her way out, just knowing which hall and which corridor to cross. The VA instead would have a map on their phone (or whatever) that they'd would have to follow if they wanted out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006443#post1006443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Baring the original Clock King, all of the versions of this character which follow the same style (Clock King II in the comics and the Flash TV show version) explicitly call this out as a form of precognition, and in the DCAU he eventually powers up significantly with a time dilating gadget... so maybe not the best example?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if you saw the version I was referencing then, because it's quite explicitly not Precognition but just expert timing in the Animated Series. I am ignorant of other iterations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006443#post1006443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that's why a lot of people find Time 1 to be so disappointing RAW. If the books supported some sort of &quot;spidey-sense&quot; level stuff (like the CofD did with Time 1), it would be a lot cooler and a lot more applicable. But as written any level of pre-cog starts at Time 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, it just seems to me like splitting hairs when one says &quot;Avoiding their punches requires looking two seconds into the future, therefore it's Time 2&quot;, especially since the minimum distance of time Time 2 works for is within a year. Just like how putting a small mark on your face requires the same sphere complexity as giving yourself wings or making your skin hard as rock. But healing yourself is not as hard.<br /> <br /> With what you're telling me, it's easier to heal a bullet wound than to change your hair colour... As a Biologist you have to admit that's rather ridiculous. Melanin in hair follicles should be easier to manipulate than all the repair mechanisms such as clotting factors, angeogenesis factors, muscle repair mechanisms... and then there's all the immune cells, the dendritic cells, the macrophages, all those activated complement molecules and triggered Toll like Receptors to subdue while still containing any invading infectious bodies introduced at the sight of the wound. And that's not even considering the blood that needs to be replaced, which in theory would mean putting erythropoietin into overdrive; or controlling all the systems that start to go out of wack from blood loss such as Shock. That adrenaline also need to be controlled and curtailed. We are talking instant &quot;everything's better&quot; after all.<br /> <br /> And yet, all of this is meant to be simpler than taking the melanin out of your hair or increasing melanin production in a localised area of your face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006443#post1006443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books are the common ground we all operate on. As noted earlier, it's still got to follow the Sphere write-ups if there isn't an official rote for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly, but not to the point of absurdity. The entire system is meant to be discussed via relative levels and piecing things where they logically or intuitively seem to fit. Thing get hazy at the borders, but that's how it should be. With my games, my main principle is &quot;if you can convince me that your effect works with the spheres that you have under the paradigm your mage believes, then we'll go with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> I guess I see it as referring to a dictionary if I want to construct a sentence. Yes your words will be technically correct, but it's somewhat stifling to be restricted to their definitions when there are so many methods of expression that can benefit from inexact use. Sometimes you really need a few cromulent words to really jigger your thoughts into place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T22:57:42-08:00","id":1006599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006480#post1006480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The mage can keep absolute track of her own Effects and timing, easily judging subjective time as necessary to put a precise duration or spin on any action.&quot;<br /> I take this to mean if you need to stop on a dime, then you can, so if you're following someone and they stop moving, you can stop along with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get that. I get, &quot;if you need to stop on a time, you know exactly how long it will take you to do so, so you know if you have time to stop or not.&quot; Knowing exactly how long it takes to do X doesn't equate to any boosts to doing X.<br /> <br /> Being able to judge exactly how long you have to cross train tracks before the train comes, and how long it will take you to do so, doesn't mean you gain a bonus to running across the tracks. It means if you can cross the tracks before the train comes, you can time it perfectly (assuming you don't trip and fall) so that nobody can follow you without getting hit by the train.<br /> <br /> Nothing in there says you can react faster to things, such as giving you a boost in a quick draw. It doesn't make you faster than the other guy. If he's faster than you he's going to shoot first. Knowing he's faster than you would be better applied to realizing you're going to need to resort to defensive tactics.<br /> <br /> Physical reaction speed doesn't change simply because adrenal perceptional skewing of time doesn't distract you any more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, see I would disagree with this point quite a bit. </div> </div> </div>Can you point to anything in any book that actually supports this? Because the examples of this all go in one of two directions: paradigm leading to increased Spheres in use, or a different combination of Spheres for a different way to the same result. Nothing I can think of ever says paradigm lets you reduce the dot levels required for an effect in any way, shape, or form.<br /> <br /> This way, to me, is the path of the Purple Jedi. &quot;Everything is possible with Mind alone, because my mind and my will directly change reality.&quot; Boosting physical Attributes? Mind 1 because that can boost mental Attributes and mind of matter means that your body is just an expression of your mind. Etc. What on Earth stops this sort of thing once you allow paradigm to modify minimum Sphere requirements?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can't use Entropy 1 for this, since there's nothing to read. </div> </div> </div>Just a note, since this is actually something you can infer from the Hollower Rev. TB (since there's a Corr/Entropy Rote for pretty much exactly this), that &quot;reading the chaos&quot; and &quot;reading fate&quot; are essentially the same thing, but from different directions. &quot;Reading fate&quot; assumes there's a destined path that you then find and follow, while &quot;reading chaos,&quot; assumes that there are infinite possible paths and you find the one that you want to follow. Both mental approaches are still just searching the available paths in the end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure if you saw the version I was referencing then, because it's quite explicitly not Precognition but just expert timing in the Animated Series. </div> </div> </div>It's been awhile. But I'm going to stand by the &quot;not the best example,&quot; since comic-book logic isn't inherently Mage logic. DCAU Batman is full of examples of things that are treated as &quot;mundane&quot; skills that would be impossible in Mage without magic. There's plenty of inspiration there, but not stuff that should be assumed to be &quot;easy&quot; or &quot;low level&quot; magic just because non-magic characters in Batman can do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just like how putting a small mark on your face requires the same sphere complexity as giving yourself wings or making your skin hard as rock. But healing yourself is not as hard. </div> </div> </div>Again, you're treating &quot;minimum Sphere rank,&quot; as the sum total of difficulty. Healing yourself doesn't require as deep an understanding of Life. That doesn't mean it's easier in terms of number of successes needed and other considerations. A 2 dot effect that needs 5 successes is not inherently &quot;easier&quot; than a 3 dot effect that needs 1 success. The system has more than one way to address this than just Sphere rank.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T13:41:35-08:00","id":1006841,"title":"","content":"To the people viewing this silly argument. Thank you for your patients.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Right, getting sick of multiple quote boxes (plus quoting people means I can't do a proper spellcheck), so I'm going to do away with that in favour of just addressing points<br /> <br /> Stop on a dime bit:<br /> Ok, fair point. Perhaps you'd need a bit of Mind 1 to sync up your reactions with your time sense.<br /> <br /> I'd argue, however, that Perfect Time is more than just &quot;knowing the amount of time it takes&quot; it's about feeling the flow of time, being able to incorporate rhythm into your senses. You can how long someone takes to run away and roughly where they'll be if they keep running at that speed, so you can adjust your aim to compensate for that and thus it's easier to shoot them as they run.<br /> <br /> Similarly in a fistfight, if you've been fighting for a while you should be able to tell the rhythm of their moves and then be able to parry and doge much more effectively. Sort of like how Studied Combat is described for the Investigator Class in Pathfinder.<br /> <br /> <br /> Paradigm and Sphere bit:<br /> Is it really any different than saying your Biologist could change hair colour with Matter 2/Life 2 instead of just Life 3?<br /> <br /> Anyway, the idea of this came from several sources.<br /> <br /> Time 3 rote Time Warp:-<br /> &quot;Naturally, this spell is so difficult and specific that very few mages use it at all. Some paradigms just don't accommodate the idea of &quot;rewinding time&quot; while others facilitate it.&quot;<br /> This is what first fuelled the idea for me that there spheres are not the same for everyone. It states that my Time 3 is not the same as another's Time 3, and that this difference in how the spheres function between mages stems from paradigm, the basic tenements in belief of what these elements of reality include and how they operate, and thus the logic should be that Paradigm and Belief should dictate how certain patterns are affects by certain spheres.<br /> <br /> Forces:-<br /> &quot;Every magical style has a different means of addressing these forces. Science considers certain forces to be the absence of others, while mystical Traditions usually consider negative and positive forces - heat and cold, light and dark, motion and stillness - to be opposite but independent entities.&quot;<br /> So if Light and Dark are independent entities, it stands to reason that you'd need Forces 3 to transform light into dark, but Forces 2 to move dark around, or move light around. Otherwise you're ignoring the mystic paradigm.<br /> <br /> Entropy:-<br /> &quot;Mages who study Entropy often choose the path of either order or chaos. Students of order look into patterns, into the ways that events flow from one to the next and into the means by which new things build on the old. Students of chaos study the dissolution of patterns, the destruction of matter and the random elements that infect happenstance and probability.&quot;<br /> So, it stands to reason that mages who are more confident with &quot;order&quot; and believe in the concept of fate will have a much easier time looking into their fate and intuiting their outcome. While mages who study &quot;chaos&quot; and think all forms of order are nothing more than an illusion would find it much more difficult to &quot;feel the fate&quot; that simply isn't there, and instead would have to force reality to give them a path.<br /> <br /> Then there's that bit in HDYDT called &quot;A bit of spirit&quot; which addresses the issue that paradigms based on &quot;all universal forces are actually spirits&quot; means that all magic a mage does is essentially Spirit magic, and so would at least need Spirit 1 in everything that they do. This too fuels the idea that paradigm shapes how the spheres are required rather than the spheres themselves defining the effects.<br /> <br /> Essentially what I'm saying is that the logic that goes behind the effect from the point of view of the mage should dictate the sphere level required, rather than just matching like-with-like rotes to sphere levels. This is also a good way to combat the ever present Purple Paradigm. If my spheres are different from your spheres, then there simply can't be a purple paradigm as our magic is inherently different by proxy of our understanding of the arts.<br /> <br /> Remember, it's not reducing or increasing sphere use, it's using the logic of the paradigm to dictate what the definitions of the sphere levels are referring to.<br /> <br /> <br /> Purple Jedi bit:<br /> Really easy way to combat this. Just like the Dream Speaker needs a bit of spirit in all their effects, your Jedi needs a bit of Mind in all of theirs. Raising Physical Attributes would therefor be a Mind1/Life1 rote for them. So yes, everything is just &quot;mind&quot; to them, but the way their mind influences &quot;Life&quot; is how they study the Life sphere and how their mind influences movement is how they study the Forces sphere. Going further, you could say that no sphere can be higher than their rank in Mind. The trade off could be that everything they are doing is still treated as a Mind effect, meaning that most of the effects are harder to detect if you're not looking for Mind patterns, or that dispelling their effects is impossible without similar ranks in Mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dot on the face bit:<br /> Problem is that the number of successes doesn't reflect the relative complexity of these tasks either.<br /> <br /> Going RAW, healing yourself for 4 points of Lethal should only require 2 Successes.<br /> Putting a dot on your face, however, would need 1 success for being a simple feat, and at least 1 other success so it lasts longer than an instant. so at least 2 successes (3 if you want it to last a day).<br /> So with healing 4 points Lethal requiring an equal amount if not fewer successes than putting a dot on your face, to say the former requires Life 2 while the latter Life 3 is to ignore biological complexity for the sake of making everything fit into these neat little sphere boxes by sheer category. And I for one think it's a shame to stifil the system in such a way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 11-22-2016, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T15:14:52-08:00","id":1006875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006841#post1006841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time 3 rote Time Warp:-<br /> &quot;Naturally, this spell is so difficult and specific that very few mages use it at all. Some paradigms just don't accommodate the idea of &quot;rewinding time&quot; while others facilitate it.&quot;<br /> This is what first fuelled the idea for me that there spheres are not the same for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but the important part here is, this does not mean that some characters get something <i>EXTRA</i> with some spheres. It's the very opposite. Many Mages do not get the whole package of a sphere level's out-of-the-book writeup. At least at first.<br /> <br /> The part you quoted essentially states what I've mentioned before in another thread about out-of-game sphere writeups and in-game paradigms:<br /> The sphere effect writeups per sphere level in the book are the combination and amalgation of everything that is possible at this sphere rank, if you combined the beliefs and paradigms of all mages into one hodgepodge.<br /> <br /> Or in other words, one paradigm might well incorporate the idea of rewinding time if a Mage has Time 3 on their sheet, while the very same Mage character (numbers-wise, and also with Time 3 on their sheet) with a different paradigm would never even think that they can manipulate time itself, and only uses the out-of-game concept of &quot;Time 3&quot; to give themself the Blessed Speed Of The Ferocious Tiger. Manipulating the actual timestream? Sillyness. That's what those crazy technomancers are trying to do.<br /> Of course other Mages might clearly see the distorted flow of time around the character...<br /> <br /> And needless to say, the possibilities the Mage has with a specific sphere level they had on their sheet for quite a while might be different after a seeking...<br /> <br /> <br /> Mage always has been a game of players voluntarily limiting their characters out of pure fluff, contrary to being limited by actual rules - it's what defines many Mage paradigms in the first place. And what makes the game so hard for many players on an purely gamer-instinctual level, compared to other RPGs.<br /> <br /> One of the hardest things to do on the part of any Mage ST is to teach new players that <i>voluntarily</i> limiting your character, despite what the hard numbers on the sheet say, can be <i>FUN.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-22-2016, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T16:33:55-08:00","id":1006899,"title":"","content":"To expand on Ambrosia's point above, let's use another example: Life manipulating bacteria. Simply put, not all Mages either believe in germ theory of disease, or have germ theory as a part of the framework of their magical style. Even if a Dreamspeaker buys into the modern idea of micro-organisms, his traditional methods don't necessarily have any tools or techniques for how to interact with them. Sickness for him is caused by bad spirits or witchcraft, so that's what he combats when he does Medicine Work. Same with the Akashic, who screws around with the flow of Chi within a person's body in order to treat or cause sickness. Whether they have a conception of extremely tiny creatures that cause illness, their old methods don't include how to affect them directly. Outside of the context of disease's effects on the body, bacteria might as well not exist.<br /> <br /> As such, unless the traditionalist works to find a theory within their Focus that explains them, they can't fool around with stuff found at the bottom of a microscope. That part of the Life Sphere is not available to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 11-22-2016, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T17:07:52-08:00","id":1006908,"title":"","content":"So, by the same token, it could be that an Ecstatic is so &quot;in the flow&quot; with their Time sense that they could do things dance around any punch thrown by their enemy. This wouldn't be possible for an Etherite who just sees their Time sense as little more than a really accurate chronometer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T20:14:00-08:00","id":1006994,"title":"","content":"OK, so I don't think we're going to get past a simple point: You can't use Paradigm to reduce the requirements for an effect.<br /> <br /> We agree that some paradigms might make things require higher dots/dots from other Spheres, or might just make certain things impossible. This addresses the whole &quot;darkness&quot; thing. <br /> <br /> The disagreement centers on the idea of, &quot;...the logic that goes behind the effect from the point of view of the mage should dictate the sphere level required, rather than just matching like-with-like rotes to sphere levels.&quot; Because this doesn't combat the Purple Paradigm or the Purple Jedi; it actually reinforces those things because it creates an out-of-character incentive to have a mage with a point of view that allows as much power as possible with as few Spheres as possible, and reduces magic to &quot;flavorless&quot; willworking.<br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> As for the whole Perfect Time thing:<br /> <br /> I just don't buy it. People don't fight with some constant rhythm you get to learn and then follow, because that's stupid even against people without magical senses. People running away from gunfire don't run in straight predictable lines if they can avoid it even without people with magical senses because that makes you easier to shoot.<br /> <br /> That's why &quot;combat Time magic&quot; starts at Time 2 to me. I could see an argument for Time 1 against a predictable system (like shooting ducks in a shooting gallery moving at a steady pace) where you can count on that. In actual fighting without that predictability, Time 1 doesn't give you anything you can actually apply. It's just like the stopping on a dime thing.<br /> <br /> Consider, for example, that aiming at a target in combat relies on them either being relatively still or moving in a slow constant fashion. You can't claim the aiming bonus against someone ducking and weaving as they run away from you. How can Time 1 overcome that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T20:52:08-08:00","id":1007010,"title":"","content":"But you can use paradigm to redefine what these requirements refer to. That's all I'm trying to impart.<br /> <br /> Regarding your player insentive problem, I'd just say that players like that are not the right kind if players for Mage in general. The character comes first, then the paradigm, then the way their paradigm fits in with the Spheres.<br /> <br /> The way I'm viewing this &quot;go with the flow&quot; idea is that Ecstatics would be able to just intuitively feel how much time they'd need to move out of the way. They can feel out and accurately judge based on much fewer indicators how much time their punches have until they make contact and what little movement try need to make in order to get avoid it all.<br /> Their time sense affords them this intuition and their dance allows them the coordination they need to respond appropriately.<br /> <br /> And if that doesn't make sense to you, then fine, it doesn't make sense to you. That's ok. Let it not make sense and disregard it. You can just keep the Etherite with her chronometer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T22:31:15-08:00","id":1007040,"title":"","content":"Here's a use of Time 1 that doesn't get talked about much: making backward time travel much less dangerous. When you've traveled back in time it's very hard to guess which things will trigger a butterfly effect type cascade with the slightest change made by you, and which will not. Time 2 can give you more specifics, but it is laborious and impractical to try to check every possible consequece for every action you do as you're doing it. Time 1 can give a quick snapshot: &quot;this moment is critical to the timestream--I should hang back a bit and find a better time to make the precise change I want.&quot; Or, &quot;this moment in time is relatively durable. I could take relatively bold action and not make too many unwanted changes.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T00:40:03-08:00","id":1007083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1007040#post1007040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a use of Time 1 that doesn't get talked about much: making backward time travel much less dangerous. When you've traveled back in time it's very hard to guess which things will trigger a butterfly effect type cascade with the slightest change made by you, and which will not. Time 2 can give you more specifics, but it is laborious and impractical to try to check every possible consequece for every action you do as you're doing it. Time 1 can give a quick snapshot: &quot;this moment is critical to the timestream--I should hang back a bit and find a better time to make the precise change I want.&quot; Or, &quot;this moment in time is relatively durable. I could take relatively bold action and not make too many unwanted changes.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be something that relies at least in part on Entropy. (The difference between time-viewing and destiny-divining is an interesting one . . . )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T02:28:31-08:00","id":1007111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1006994#post1006994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We agree that some paradigms might make things require higher dots/dots from other Spheres</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I disagree with paradigms possibly giving something extra on top of the current sphere writeups without adding something completely new like the Primal Utility Sphere, I ALSO disagree with this idea.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, the sphere abilities should be seen as something 'neutral'. The Dark Ages pillars were all about different hard mechanics between factions to achieve the same effects.<br /> <br /> Yes, some paradigms might not allow an effect that a specific sphere level has in the RAW, simply because that kind of effect does not at all fit into the paradigm's worldview..but that's it. If a paradigm allows &quot;manipulation of haircolor&quot;, Life 3 should be enough for doing that, no matter *how* the paradigm actually explains the modification in in-game words. Changing part of a life pattern is changing part of a life pattern, even if the paradigm scientifically says 'hair is dead matter'.<br /> <br /> It makes things OOCly fair and simple for the players. Let's not add a 'Yes, the sphere says you can do X, but YOU also need Sphere Y..'. HDYDT already went off the rails with that.<br /> <br /> How the characters think they are doing it, in-game, is a different matter. And it's the same reason why, for example, Life AND Matter are always required to hurt and change a vampire, no matter if a character's paradigm says &quot;vampire bodies are just dead matter&quot;, or defines it as something mystical.<br /> <br /> <br /> HOWEVER:<br /> I agree that for some paradigms certain things can be harder to pull off than for other paradigms, even if both paradigms allow a feat.<br /> And we already have a mechanism for that: It's called instruments.<br /> <br /> <br /> Turning into a different human? Piece of cake for a Verbena Lifeweaver. A practiced, short ritual, simple gestures, carvings, and BAM. You're done.<br /> For the average Progenitor surgeon? A surgery op, with tools, computers and what have you, requiring a good location and those items.<br /> <br /> <br /> The same goes for using Time 2 to predict a combatant's next moves. Clairvoyancy.<br /> A Dreamspeaker or Oracle-of-Deplhi style Mage? It's next to impossible for them to do in combat. They require their rituals, chants, a body of water or ecstatic kneeling over a natural gas fissure, and their clairvoyancy only lasts while performing that. Their kind of clairvoyancy simply does not fit combat.<br /> A Cultist of Ecstasy? Well, if we go by the average stereotype among them, they enter combat high as a kite and go to town.<br /> <br /> <br /> Several paradigms, the same allowed magickal concepts, but big difficulty differences simply based on *how* they get to what they're trying to achieve - without any differences in required spheres needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-23-2016, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T03:25:49-08:00","id":1007130,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> the spheres aren't changing based on paradigm though.<br /> <br /> Forces two is still &quot;amplify&quot; and Only Forcese 3 is &quot;change&quot;.<br /> The paradigm just states what is being amplified &quot;light, dark, or photons&quot; and thus when forces 3 is required to instil change &quot;change light to dark&quot;<br /> <br /> The spheres aren't actually changeing, but their preview is.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Life two affects simple patterns and heals the self, so maybe hair colour is seen as a simple pattern that is part if the self and so fits under Life 2.<br /> <br /> Again, not changeing the sphere, just altering the descriptions of other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T03:40:40-08:00","id":1007138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1007130#post1007130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, not changeing the sphere, just altering the descriptions of other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going by Heavy Arms' quote of different paradigms requiring <i>different spheres</i> or <i>different sphere levels</i> for the <i>same(!) magickal effect</i>.<br /> I disagree.<br /> <br /> But yes, a paradigm can <i>limit</i> what a sphere can do at a specific level, simply because the described effect is just not possible in a certain paradigm's worldview. I've made that point two posts ago <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, Life two affects simple patterns and heals the self, so maybe hair colour is seen as a simple pattern that is part if the self and so fits under Life 2. </div> </div> </div>It's not a 'maybe'.<br /> You want to directly, <i>magically literally cause hair itself to change color out of nowhere</i>, and your paradigm allows this to happen?<br /> Then you can always use Life 2, as the sphere description says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or perform small alterations (hair color, skin tone, height, weight, and so on) to his basic form. </div> </div> </div>It does not matter if your paradigm says '<i>Hairs are dead matter</i>' or not. You need Life 2. It's independent of how the character explains to themselves what is actually happening. It's always a metaphysical change of a lifepattern. See my last post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Is it possible to get changed hair color with other spheres?<br /> Yes. Absolutely. Use Prime and Matter to conjure tiny droplets of color onto your hair. Magickal Hairspray for the win.<br /> <br /> But in that case the literal, paradigm-enabled magickal effect is not 'Change hair color'. The literal magickal effect is 'conjure drops of color out of nowhere'. They just happen to land on the hair.<br /> <br /> A paradigm that does not allow 'haircolor changing on its own' will never allow you to use Life 2 for it.<br /> A paradigm that does not allow 'conjuration of drops of color' will never allow using Prime+Matter.<br /> The end result will be the same though.<br /> <br /> But neither case actually changes the sphere requirements of 'haircolor changing on its own' or 'conjuration of drops of color'.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> And to add, I might have misunderstood Heavy Arms wrong in his quote...since..<br /> Yes, a character who believes 'conjuring darkness' being a thing uses different spheres to do so, than a character who believes that darkness is an absence of light.<br /> <br /> But that's not because they require different spheres for the same magickal effect - it's because they are actually performing different magical effects to have a blob of darkness filling the room <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-23-2016, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T04:02:28-08:00","id":1007151,"title":"","content":"TL;DR'ing myself:<br /> <br /> 1) Different paradigms might require you to perform different magickal effects to achieve the same same end result<br /> 2) This is because a paradigm might not allow the Mage to perform a specific magickal effect, despite a Sphere level in RAW generally allowing it. Overcoming that is part of shifts in paradigm.<br /> 3) The very same magical effect always requires the very same sphere and sphere level.<br /> 4) Even if different paradigms allow for the very same magical effect, some paradigms make it easier or harder to perform the magickal effect because of the instruments and situations required.<br /> 5) Do not mistake a magical effect for its end result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-23-2016, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T06:00:10-08:00","id":1007192,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> <br /> <br /> Very well. Though I would say that the methods behind the effect will detail the caveats of the result.<br /> <br /> For example, if a Hermetic used Force 2 to expand the darkness to fill the room, then the light would still be there somewhere, pushed aside. This might mean there within the darkness pockets of intense light might be found. This is ofcourse unless they move the light around as well, perhaps putting all the light into one localised point or doing a complicated spell which both lowers light and increases dark.<br /> An Etherite decreasing the number of photons in the area, on the other hand, would not have such difficulties. However, depending on where the photons they throw away end up, if they happen to bounce into the eyes of random passers by, they may get strange visions of colour and, if the photons were removed wholesale, would give people the impression that they were in a holographic room of sorts. An effect that Hermetics may only consider Mind mages capable of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T06:10:25-08:00","id":1007197,"title":"","content":"Just voicing my agreement with Ambrosia. His view is exactly how we have always interpreted spheres and paradigm. The mage's belief of how a sphere is changing reality does not change the sphere level in game mechanics for doing so. That would be grossly unfair. However it most certainly will change the time and tools required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T21:41:44-08:00","id":1007554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1007138#post1007138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to add, I might have misunderstood Heavy Arms wrong in his quote...since..<br /> Yes, a character who believes 'conjuring darkness' being a thing uses different spheres to do so, than a character who believes that darkness is an absence of light.<br /> <br /> But that's not because they require different spheres for the same magickal effect - it's because they are actually performing different magical effects to have a blob of darkness filling the room <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is what I was trying to get at. Thank you for taking the time to re-parse that out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T22:40:20-08:00","id":1007576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005695-examples-of-time-1?p=1007083#post1007083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems to be something that relies at least in part on Entropy. (The difference between time-viewing and destiny-divining is an interesting one . . . )</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree that you need Entropy 1 to gauge a moment's actual <i>significance</i>, but Time 1 should be enough to tell how much changing a particular moment could affect the future [edit: actually the present and past, but the future from the time traveler's current perspective] in large but meaningless ways that would still bring a lot of Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 11-24-2016, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}